WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:07.760
The pet food industry has received unkind remarks as to the true origin of its ingredients for decades.
几十年来，宠物食品行业在原料的真正来源问题上一直饱受尖刻的非议。

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:17.090
Now the industry faces another source of criticism as a new book starts a debate about the environmental impact of owning a well-fed pet.
如今，随着一本新书引发了一场关于“养一只吃得好的宠物会对环境造成什么影响”的争论，这个行业又多了一个招致批评的缘由。

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:35.470
The New Scientist magazine, in a recent editorial, largely agreed with the book’s findings that some pets, due to the food they eat, have a surprisingly high “ecological footprint”, which is a way of quantifying human demand on the planet’s ecosystems using a measure called “global hectares”.
《新科学家》杂志在最近的一篇社论中基本认同这本书的研究结论：一些宠物由于所吃的食物，“生态足迹”高得出人意料。“生态足迹”是一种量化人类对地球生态系统需求的方法，所用的计量单位叫作“全球公顷”。

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:46.990
According to the authors of the book, “A shocking comparison is that in 2004, the average citizen of some poor countries had an eco-footprint of 0.76 hectares.
据这本书的作者称：“一个令人震惊的对比是：2004年，一些贫穷国家普通公民的生态足迹为0.76公顷。

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:58.880
The eco-footprint of a medium-sized dog is about 0.84 hectares, and that of a cat is about 0.15 hectares, almost the same as what is needed to run a small car.
一只中型犬的生态足迹约为0.84公顷，一只猫的约为0.15公顷，几乎和开一辆小汽车所需的一样多。

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:07.160
In a world where resources are already limited, can people really justify keeping pets that require more than some people do?”
在一个资源本已有限的世界里，人们饲养所需资源比一些人还多的宠物，真的说得过去吗？”

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:14.370
The authors of the book say that they were “genuinely surprised” when calculating the environmental impact of pets.
这本书的作者说，他们在计算宠物对环境的影响时“真的很吃惊”。

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:20.300
And some of the ideas they put forward to attenuate this are likely to shock some pet owners.
而他们为减轻这种影响提出的一些主张，很可能会让一些宠物主人震惊。

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:32.240
For example, the book suggests catching pests such as field mice and processing them into a “natural” cat food, or raising pets like chickens that provide both company and fresh eggs.
例如，书中建议捕捉田鼠之类的有害动物，把它们加工成“天然”猫粮；或者饲养像鸡这样既能作伴、又能提供新鲜鸡蛋的宠物。

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:42.040
When feeding a pet, however, owners are advised to favour pet foods made from chicken meat, which is less damaging to the environment than red meat and fish.
不过，在喂养宠物时，建议主人优先选择用鸡肉制成的宠物食品，因为鸡肉对环境的危害比红肉和鱼肉小。

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:58.010
As you might expect, the Pet Food Manufacturers Association (PFMA) puts up a spirited defence, arguing that the vast majority of meat and fish used in pet foods is of sufficient quality for human consumption but surplus to human needs.
或许不出你所料，宠物食品制造商协会（PFMA）进行了有力的辩护，称宠物食品中使用的肉和鱼绝大多数品质都足以供人类食用，只是超出了人类的需求。

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:07.960
“If we didn’t recycle animal by-products to sell, they might instead be abandoned and buried under the earth, which is not very green,” says the PFMA’s director.
“如果我们不把动物副产品回收利用起来出售，它们就可能会被丢弃、埋到地下，那可不怎么环保，”该协会的负责人说。

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:13.680
In addition, he points out that pets should not be judged just on their carbon footprint.
此外，他指出，不应该仅凭碳足迹来评判宠物。

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:18.020
“Our environment is greatly enriched by the part they play in our lives.
“宠物在我们生活中所起的作用极大地丰富了我们的环境。

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:24.740
Pets in the home inspire responsibility, encourage social awareness and have positive health benefits.”
家里的宠物能激发责任感，增强社会意识，还对健康有积极作用。”
